  EXACT all-prime handling (the (sigma-1)-handling):
    identity: prod_p (1+p^-sigma) = prod_p (1-p^-2sigma)/(1-p^-sigma)
             = zeta(sigma)/zeta(2sigma)   (sigma > 1)   [exact]
    -> M_full(sigma) = ln zeta(sigma) - ln zeta(2sigma)  (exact, all primes)
    -> as sigma -> 1+:  M_full(sigma) = -ln(sigma-1) - ln zeta(2) + o(1)
       residue EXACT: C = -ln zeta(2) = -0.49770030247074534747
    sigma=1.001: M_full=    6.411770   M_cut(10^6)=    1.962846   (missing tail +4.448924)
    sigma=1.010: M_full=    4.124458   M_cut(10^6)=    1.898288   (missing tail +2.226170)
    sigma=1.050: M_full=    2.579536   M_cut(10^6)=    1.653922   (missing tail +0.925615)
    sigma=1.100: M_full=    1.960245   M_cut(10^6)=    1.422234   (missing tail +0.538011)
    sigma=1.500: M_full=    0.776226   M_cut(10^6)=    0.654502   (missing tail +0.121724)
    sigma=2.000: M_full=    0.418590   M_cut(10^6)=    0.355316   (missing tail +0.063275)
    -> the cutoff sum is exact for sigma >= ~1.5 (tail < 2e-4) and misses
       the logarithmically divergent tail for sigma -> 1+; R below uses M_full.

